<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-14894] Parallel pass2 support for e2fsck</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-14894</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-8465" title="parallel e2fsck performance at scale" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-8465"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-8465&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; implemented parallel inode table scanning for e2fsck pass1, and parallel bitmap loading for e2fsck pass5.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;After these improvements, e2fsck of a 50% full 1PB filesystem running with 256 threads improved pass1 from 7777s to 191s (40x faster), and pass5 from 10523s to 286s (36x faster).  &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;However, pass2 only improved marginally, from 1363s to 1265s (7%) and this now dominates the total e2fsck runtime (70% in this test) on large OSTs, and limits the aggregate speedup of e2fsck to "only" 10x faster despite the other improvements.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Processing directories in parallel should also be possible, in order to further speed up e2fsck times on large OSTs, and expecially on large MDT filesystems.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment />
